WEBVTT

00:00.300 --> 00:05.460
To plan your dives and your minimum gas, you need one number: your surface consumption rate, SCR.

00:06.600 --> 00:08.490
It is a key part of gas planning.

00:10.170 --> 00:13.030
SCR is the litres you breathe per minute at the surface.

00:13.962 --> 00:17.522
It is also called SAC, surface air consumption.

00:17.582 --> 00:22.292
But we do not always breathe air, because the gas can be nitrox or trimix.

00:24.392 --> 00:29.912
For example, in our dive the average depth is twenty metres, and the dive lasts thirty-five minutes.

00:29.912 --> 00:35.042
The tank holds eleven point one litres, and its pressure went from two hundred bar to sixty bar.

00:36.792 --> 00:40.472
Step one: let's calculate the gas you used, in bar.

00:40.592 --> 00:43.702
Two hundred bar minus sixty bar is one hundred and forty bar.

00:45.152 --> 00:47.972
Step two: let's calculate the same gas in litres.

00:48.132 --> 00:54.792
One hundred and forty bar times the tank's volume, eleven point one litres, is one thousand five hundred and fifty-four litres.

00:57.162 --> 01:00.642
Step three: let's calculate the gas you used per minute, at depth.

01:00.642 --> 01:06.982
One thousand five hundred and fifty-four litres divided by thirty-five minutes is forty-four point four litres per minute.

01:08.382 --> 01:10.962
Step four: let's calculate the average pressure.

01:11.042 --> 01:14.512
Twenty metres divided by ten, plus one, is three atmospheres.

01:15.762 --> 01:20.022
Step five: let's calculate your SCR, the rate at the surface.

01:20.342 --> 01:27.502
Forty-four point four litres per minute divided by three atmospheres is fourteen point eight, rounded up to fifteen litres per minute.

01:30.612 --> 01:38.132
Collect your own SCR over several dives, in different conditions, and plan with a high value, not the average, rounded up.

01:39.152 --> 01:43.032
Until you have measured your own SCR, start with twenty litres per minute.

01:43.032 --> 01:46.172
This table shows the bar you use every five minutes.

01:47.049 --> 01:51.759
If you find your consumption is higher than twenty litres per minute, plan with your own number.

01:54.859 --> 02:00.579
Some dive computers calculate your SCR from the tank pressure a transmitter sends.

02:01.450 --> 02:07.650
For Shearwater divers, Dive log shows it for each dive, and soon how it changes over time.

02:07.830 --> 02:09.730
Free on the App Store.

02:10.601 --> 02:12.011
diver dot today.
